1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,840
What if you grew one centimetre every

2
00:00:01,840 --> 00:00:02,880
single second?

3
00:00:02,880 --> 00:00:04,160
That sounds slow.

4
00:00:04,160 --> 00:00:06,000
A centimetre is about as wide as

5
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:06,880
a fingernail.

6
00:00:06,880 --> 00:00:08,000
But watch the clock.

7
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:08,720
After one minute,

8
00:00:08,720 --> 00:00:10,560
you're sixty centimetres taller.

9
00:00:10,560 --> 00:00:11,520
Your trousers,

10
00:00:11,520 --> 00:00:12,000
sadly,

11
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:12,560
are not.

12
00:00:12,560 --> 00:00:13,760
In under two minutes,

13
00:00:13,760 --> 00:00:15,840
you're taller than the tallest human ever

14
00:00:15,840 --> 00:00:16,480
recorded.

15
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:18,000
That was Robert Wadlow,

16
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:19,840
at two point seven two metres.

17
00:00:19,840 --> 00:00:21,200
Congratulations.

18
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:22,720
You now need a new front door.

19
00:00:22,720 --> 00:00:23,520
After an hour,

20
00:00:23,520 --> 00:00:25,360
you're thirty-six metres taller,

21
00:00:25,360 --> 00:00:27,040
about a twelve-storey building.

22
00:00:27,040 --> 00:00:28,160
Here's the catch.

23
00:00:28,160 --> 00:00:29,680
Double your height and your weight

24
00:00:29,680 --> 00:00:31,120
multiplies by eight,

25
00:00:31,120 --> 00:00:32,960
but your bones only get four times

26
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:33,680
stronger.

27
00:00:33,680 --> 00:00:35,280
So past three metres or so,

28
00:00:35,280 --> 00:00:36,720
you'd probably collapse.

29
00:00:36,720 --> 00:00:38,640
Your heart would also struggle to pump

30
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:40,000
blood all the way up.

31
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:41,360
Let's pretend your bones,

32
00:00:41,360 --> 00:00:43,120
heart and lungs all keep up.

33
00:00:43,120 --> 00:00:43,840
In a day,

34
00:00:43,840 --> 00:00:45,920
you'd be taller than the Burj Khalifa.

35
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:46,720
In ten days,

36
00:00:46,720 --> 00:00:48,240
you'd tower over Everest,

37
00:00:48,240 --> 00:00:49,520
with your head in air too thin

38
00:00:49,520 --> 00:00:50,240
to breathe.

39
00:00:50,240 --> 00:00:51,040
In four months,

40
00:00:51,040 --> 00:00:52,640
your head pokes into space.

41
00:00:52,640 --> 00:00:54,320
And in about twelve hundred years,

42
00:00:54,320 --> 00:00:56,000
you'd finally touch the Moon.

43
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:57,760
The hardest part would still be finding

44
00:00:57,760 --> 00:00:59,180
trousers.
